+
+## 8. Replay set (M1 n-gram) — `replay_manifest.json` (built by `bench/build_replay_set.py`)
+
+Built from the host-recorded pi event streams and mem0 SQLite stores; output at
+`bench/results/2026-10-12/m1-ngram/replay_manifest.json` (committed, no raw
+content). Replay bodies live in gitignored `bench/.replay/m1/{agent,mem}.jsonl`.
+
+**Composition.** 42 replay requests total:
+
+- **agent**: 30 requests, 6 distinct run/step pairs (≥ 4 required), drawn from
+  both the baseline and mem0 arms.
+- **mem**: 12 requests (in the 6–12 range), 5 distinct run/step pairs, mem0 arm
+  only (tool-add + auto-capture events, per-call cutoffs).
+
+Every entry carries `recorded_prompt_tokens`; `n_messages_mismatches: []` (rebuilt
+`n_messages` == recorded `n_messages` for all 42). `system_prompt_exact: true`
+(sections joined by blank lines; join inferred — see manifest `system_prompt_note`).
+
+**est/recorded calibration (chars/4 estimator).**
+
+- agent median `est_over_recorded` = **0.833** (in the 0.75–1.33 band)
+- mem median `est_over_recorded` = **1.027** (in the band)
+- First-turn requests (n_messages ≤ 3) sit at 0.846–0.877, so the estimator is
+  well calibrated when the prompt is just system + tools + a single user turn
+  with no accumulated reasoning.
+
+**Outliers (est_over_recorded < 0.75).** Exactly three, all `baseline-r0/0` late
+turns that accumulate large `reasoning_content` plus tool output:
+
+| id | n_msg | est/recorded | reasoning chars | recorded tokens | no-reasoning ratio |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| inventory-baseline-r0/0/5 | 13 | 0.740 | 25,717 | 13,032 | 0.246 |
+| inventory-baseline-r0/0/8 | 19 | 0.743 | 26,225 | 13,939 | 0.272 |
+| inventory-baseline-r0/0/10 | 23 | 0.742 | 26,591 | 14,317 | 0.278 |
+
+These dip just below 0.75 because the accumulated reasoning and the test/file
+**tool output are token-dense** — code, JSON and symbols tokenize to fewer than
+4 chars per token, so the recorded token count exceeds the chars/4 estimate.
+That is expected, **not** a content-missing sign: with reasoning excluded the
+same three requests fall to 0.246 / 0.272 / 0.278, i.e. reasoning is the bulk
+of the recorded prompt and it is faithfully present in the replay bodies
+(`chars_by_role.reasoning` is non-zero and tracks the recorded prompt growth, e.g.
+`baseline-r0/0` 2,761 → 13,939 tokens across turns). All other 39 agent requests
+and all 12 mem requests are in-band.
+
+**Thinking / `reasoning_content` mechanism.** Recorded thinking blocks carry
+`thinkingSignature='reasoning_content'` (`recon/event_samples.json` — 13 occurrences
+across `turn_end` and `agent_end` sample messages, including the line-457 sample
+the standing facts cite). The replay builder keeps each assistant `reason` block
+as a `reasoning_content` field on the assistant message (mirroring pi-ai's
+openai-completions converter), which is exactly what lifts the agent median from
+0.457 (reasoning dropped) to 0.833 (reasoning kept) and matches the recorded
+prompt growth. The first-run `show_pi_ai_source()` printed an empty candidate list
+because the hardcoded `@earendil-works/**/providers/openai-completions.js` glob
+didn't match the installed layout; the search was broadened (below) to the
+`pi_package_dir` scope from `recon/sources.txt`. The empirical evidence above —
+the signature in the recorded traffic plus the 0.457 → 0.833 jump when reasoning
+is included — already confirms reasoning is sent back under `reasoning_content`.
+
+**Probe requirement.** The manifest records `server_requirement`: the probe
+llama-server needs `--jinja` (the production entry has it) so the chat template
+renders `reasoning_content` on assistant messages. Replayed agent traffic is
+text-only, so the spec/mmproj incompatibility (`bench/m1-notes.md` §3, standing
+fact) does not apply.
+
+**Status (this round).** All acceptance criteria for the replay-set item are
+met: `.gitignore` has `bench/.replay/`, the manifest lists 30 agent / 12 mem
+requests from ≥ 4 distinct steps, every entry has `recorded_prompt_tokens`, both
+medians are in 0.75–1.33, and outliers are documented here. A re-run is being
+submitted to regenerate the manifest and to finally capture the pi-ai
+source lines from the broadened `show_pi_ai_source()`, if the file resolves.
